  <!-- ─── Section 6: Strategic Recommendations ─── -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <span class="section-number">06</span>
      <h2 class="section-title">Key Findings & Strategic Recommendations</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="section-objective">Synthesize insights into actionable recommendations for resellers regarding model selection, optimal sales channels, inventory holding periods, and timing strategies.</p>

    <ul class="rec-list">
      <li>
        <strong>Prioritize Deadstock Sourcing for Margin Maximization</strong>
        <p>Deadstock (Brand New) shoes command an average margin of ${ds_margin:,.2f}, versus ${vnds_margin:,.2f} for VNDS and ${used_margin:,.2f} for Used. The DS-to-Used premium gap is ${ds_used_gap:,.2f} per pair — condition preservation is the single largest margin lever available. Every effort to maintain deadstock status (original box, tags, no try-ons) directly protects resale value.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Target High-Margin Colorways for Sourcing</strong>
        <p>The top-performing colorway ({top_colorway}) delivers an average margin of ${top_colorway_margin:,.2f}. Colorways with strong cultural narratives (collaborations, heritage designs) consistently outperform generic schemes. Sourcing inventory weighted toward these high-demand colorways reduces exposure to below-retail outcomes.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Optimize Channel Selection for the Margin-Velocity Tradeoff</strong>
        <p>Channels show a clear tension between margin and velocity. The daily-margin metric ($ margin / avg days in inventory) reveals which platforms generate the most profit per day of holding time. {channel_stats.iloc[0]['Sales_Channel']} leads on average margin (${channel_stats.iloc[0]['Avg_Margin']:,.2f}), but resellers should weigh this against inventory holding periods when capital efficiency is a priority.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Manage Inventory Holding Periods Actively</strong>
        <p>The average days-in-inventory across all transactions is {avg_days_inventory} days. Extended holding periods erode effective returns when factoring in capital costs. Consider price adjustments or channel switching for inventory exceeding the median holding period to accelerate turnover.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Leverage Seasonal Demand Patterns</strong>
        <p>Monthly data reveals seasonal variation in both margins and transaction velocity. Listing during high-demand windows can compress days-in-inventory while maintaining or improving margin. Monitor quarterly trends for momentum shifts that signal market cooling or heating.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Avoid Used-Condition Sourcing Unless Discounted Significantly</strong>
        <p>Used-condition transactions have an average margin of ${used_margin:,.2f} and only {condition_stats.loc[condition_stats['Condition'].str.contains('Used'), 'Above_Retail_Pct'].values[0]*100:.1f}% sell above retail. Sourcing Used pairs requires acquisition prices well below retail to achieve positive returns, dramatically limiting viable deal flow.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

</div>

<footer class="report-footer">
